# ⛔ ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST. Inverted 2026-07-26 08:34, and it is the third time this bit.
#
# The old shape listed the private files by name. A denylist only ever covers what existed when it
# was written — so every new strategy doc was PUBLIC BY DEFAULT until I remembered to add it.
# I wrote a comment at 07:26 saying exactly that and calling the inversion a rested job.
# An hour later there were SEVEN untracked private files on a Pages repo: THE-ASK-LIST.md, four
# pre-written asks with real people's names and my private read on each, the creator draft, and
# asks-scored.json. Predicted, then walked into, on schedule.
#
# Now: everything is ignored, and the handful that are genuinely public are named explicitly.
# A new private file is private by DEFAULT instead of by memory.

*

# --- the public site, and nothing else ---
!index.html
!terms.html
!privacy.html
!refunds.html
!2257.html
!404.html
!the-back-room.html
!robots.txt
!sitemap.xml
# !CNAME  ⛔ HELD OUT 09:18 — see below
!.gitignore

# blog: the directory and its pages only
!blog/
!blog/*.html

# ⛔ Anything not listed above does not ship. If a new page needs to be public, ADD IT HERE —
# that one line is the whole cost, and it is paid once, deliberately, instead of remembered forever.

# ⛔ CNAME IS DELIBERATELY NOT SHIPPED (09:18 2026-07-26). Kept on disk as CNAME.hold.
# A CNAME file makes GitHub Pages 301 the WORKING github.io URL to the custom domain. The custom
# domain is still on Porkbun's parking A records, and the parking service returns 200 on every path
# — so adding CNAME took the site from "reachable at github.io" to "reachable nowhere", while every
# status-code check kept saying 200. Restore it the moment the apex A records point at GitHub.

# storefront preview art — public by design (allowlist, one line paid once)
!img/
!img/*.png
